      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(¬A∧¬B)∨(¬A∧C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can factor out the conjunction with $¬A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(¬A∧¬B)∨(¬A∧C)≡¬A∧(¬B∨C)\n$$",
